   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "OUTFIT SWAP\n\n1. Picture 1: the person. Their face, hair, expression, pose, hands and background stay.\n2. Picture 2: the outfit. A flat-lay, a product photo or another person wearing it.\n3. Press Run.\n\nOnly the clothes and shoes change. To change just one piece, edit the prompt, e.g. 'replace only the jacket with the jacket from <image2>'.\n\nTips\n- Start ComfyUI with  comfyui h3  (the --fast-disk mode): the text encoder then runs on the GPU in ~30 s instead of ~5 min on the CPU.\n- Any picture size works: the size nodes shrink it to the megapixels you set. 1.0 is fast; 1.5 is sharper but slower.\n- Seed is random each Run. Press Run again for a different take.\n- Clear, front-lit photos where the face is big enough give the best results."
   ],
   "title": "How to use",
   "color": "#b06634",
   "bgcolor": "#353535",
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "OUTFIT SWAP\n\n1. Picture 1: the person. Their face, hair, expression, pose, hands and background stay.\n2. Picture 2: the outfit. A flat-lay, a product photo or another person wearing it.\n3. Press Run.\n\nOnly the clothes and shoes change. To change just one piece, edit the prompt, e.g. 'replace only the jacket with the jacket from <image2>'.\n\nTips\n- Start ComfyUI with  comfyui h3  (the --fast-disk mode): the text encoder then runs on the GPU in ~30 s instead of ~5 min on the CPU.\n- Any picture size works: the size nodes shrink it to the megapixels you set. 1.0 is fast; 1.5 is sharper but slower.\n- Seed is random each Run. Press Run again for a different take.\n- Clear, front-lit photos where the face is big enough give the best results."
   }
  },
